// Prisma schema — HMIS Cameroon (SIGH/DME prototype)
// Registers: D-003 (PostgreSQL + Prisma), D-009 (FCFA stored as integers),
//            D-011 (hospital-scoped data access from day 1).
//
// FOUNDATIONS STEP (build steps 1-2): the schema is intentionally MINIMAL/EMPTY.
// No domain models yet — Hospital, User, Role, Patient, Encounter, Consultation,
// Invoice, InvoiceItem, Payment, AuditLog and the numbering Sequence are added in
// Step 3+ per 05_Logical_Data_Model_v0 and 07_Demo_Scenario_and_Fake_Dataset.
//
// Architecture rule (09 §4/§8): money is stored as INTEGER FCFA (no floats); every
// operational record will carry `hospital_id` and is only reachable within its
// hospital context through the data-access layer (server/db). The UI never calls
// Prisma directly.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}
